 <iati-activity default-currency="GBP" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301143-104</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria Humanitarian Response Programme: Internal Risk Facility - Undisclosed Partner SHRP B</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme is designed to address the multifaceted challenges faced by children in camps and communities in East Syria, particularly those deprived of liberty, children impacted by conflict, and internally displaced children. The proposed action is aligned with SCI&#x2019;s 2030 vision to ensure that all children in Syria survive, learn, and are protected.

The programme will take a holistic approach, adopting a socio ecological model, integrating protection, education, and economic empowerment services and addressing the needs of the most marginalized children, including those in detention centres, camps, and vulnerable communities hosting returnees or individuals resettling from camps. These efforts will be complemented by evidence-based advocacy, promoting a multi-track approach aimed at supporting the basic needs of children deprived of liberty, while advocating to fulfil their rights by fostering long term solutions and pathways out of detention centres and camps, as well as working to prevent children from being detained in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
